# The web deploy uploads the workspace, so everything the build does not read stays out of it.
# Without this the upload is ~13 GB: anchor/ alone is 6.5 GB of Rust build output and web/.next
# another 5 GB of a local production build Vercel rebuilds from source anyway.
#
# EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. These match like .gitignore patterns, so a bare
# `data` excludes *any* directory named data at any depth — including web/src/components/data,
# which is exactly what broke the first production build (Can't resolve '@/components/data').
/anchor
/web/.next
/data
/live
/docs
/context
/reference
/reference-sources
/refs
/.claude
/.review
/.21st
/.codex
/.agents
/.cursor
/.windsurf
/.surfpool
/_bmad
/_bmad-output
